{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Who</b> — the construction is <b>from Zion</b>, as: \"the scepter of your might HaShem sends <b>from Zion</b>\" and \"<b>from Zion</b> He shall sustain you,\" because the Glory was with the Ark in the days of David. And it is possible: that people of Israel were taken captive, or it refers to the future, and the meaning is: from Zion the Glory shall return, and <b>Who gives</b> is in the manner of <b>Who gives</b> — \"all the people of HaShem [were] prophets.\""], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:17.088512956Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}